## Scatter / Bubble

{% gridExampleRunner title="Scatter / Bubble" name="scatter-bubble"  exampleHeight=850 /%}

**More Details:**

- [Scatter Series](https://www.ag-grid.com/charts/javascript/scatter-series/)
- [Bubble Series](https://www.ag-grid.com/charts/javascript/bubble-series/)

### Paired Mode

Scatter and bubble charts assign the selected columns to X, Y and size values in one of two modes.

- **Paired** (default): columns alternate between X and Y values, and between X, Y and size values for bubble charts.
- **Unpaired**: the first column provides the X values and every other column is plotted against it as Y values. For bubble charts, the remaining columns alternate between Y and size values.

Users switch modes with the "Paired Mode" toggle in the Set Up (Data) tab of the chart tool panel.

Set the `paired` option on `createRangeChart()` to choose the mode when creating a chart:

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
api.createRangeChart({
    chartType: 'scatter',
    cellRange: { columns: ['gold', 'silver', 'bronze'] },
    paired: false,
});
```

Change the mode of an existing chart with `updateChart()`:

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
api.updateChart({
    type: 'rangeChartUpdate',
    chartId,
    paired: false,
});
```

The mode is saved as `paired` on the `ChartModel` returned by `getChartModels()`, so `restoreChart()` keeps it. See [Range Chart API](./integrated-charts-api-range-chart/) and [Save / Restore Charts](./integrated-charts-api-save-restore-charts/).

